# Every checkout gets LF, on every platform. Without this line a Windows
# checkout follows core.autocrlf, which defaults to true and writes CRLF into a
# working tree the repository holds as LF.
#
# Two things break on CRLF. Git hooks are run by sh, which reads the trailing \r
# as part of the command and reports a command not found for a command that is
# plainly there. And .editorconfig declares end_of_line = lf; a checkout that
# says otherwise makes that declaration a lie in the one place tools read it.
* text=auto eol=lf
